	<section data-legal-id="withdrawal">
		<h2>Withdrawal</h2>
		<div>
			Pursuant to article L 221-18 of the French Consumer Code, the user has a period of fourteen (14) clear days to withdraw, without having to give any reason. This period runs from the day after receipt of the goods for sales of goods, and from the day after acceptance of the offer for service contracts. If it expires on a Saturday, Sunday, or public holiday, it is extended to the next working day.
			<br>
			By validating a service whose immediate performance they request, the private user agrees that we begin it before the end of the period and remains liable for the amount corresponding to what has been provided up to their withdrawal.
			<br>
			Pursuant to article L 221-28 of the French Consumer Code, the withdrawal right cannot be exercised for digital content supplied on an intangible medium whose performance has begun after the user's prior express consent and express waiver of that right, which is the case for digital items made available for download as soon as payment is validated. Nor can it be exercised for goods made to the user's specifications or clearly personalised, or for services fully performed before the end of the period with the user's prior express consent.
			<br>
			The withdrawal procedure is as follows:
		</div>
		<ol>
			<li>Notify us of the withdrawal decision by an unambiguous statement, by contacting us or using the form below</li>
			<li>Validation of the request by our services</li>
			<li>Return of the goods, where applicable, under the conditions described in the Returns section</li>
			<li>Acceptance and refund to the payment method used for the defined amount
				<strong>OR</strong>
				rejection of the request with explanations</li>
		</ol>
